### GraphQL HTTP Client (Rider)
### Uso rapido: clique no botao "Run" acima de cada request.
### Porta padrao encontrada em `Properties/launchSettings.json`: 5200

@baseUrl = http://localhost:5200
@graphqlUrl = {{baseUrl}}/graphql
@newCategoryName = Gaming
@newProductName = Mouse Gamer Pro

### 0) Smoke test simples
POST {{graphqlUrl}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "query": "query { __typename }"
}

### 1) Listar produtos (equivalente a GET /products no REST)
POST {{graphqlUrl}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "query": "query { products { id name price category { id name } } }"
}

### 2) Criar categoria (addCategory)
### Salva o ID retornado em variavel global: createdCategoryId
POST {{graphqlUrl}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "query": "mutation { addCategory(name: \"Gaming\") { id name } }",
  "variables": {
    "name": "{{newCategoryName}}"
  }
}

> {%
  client.global.set("createdCategoryId", response.body.data.addCategory.id);
%}

### 3) Criar produto na categoria criada acima
### Se preferir, troque categoryId para 1 (Electronics)
POST {{graphqlUrl}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "query": "mutation($name: String!, $price: Decimal!, $categoryId: Int!) { addProduct(name: $name, price: $price, categoryId: $categoryId) { id name price category { id name } } }",
  "variables": {
    "name": "{{newProductName}}",
    "price": 199.90,
    "categoryId": {{createdCategoryId}}
  }
}

> {%
  client.global.set("createdProductId", response.body.data.addProduct.id);
%}

### 4) Atualizar produto
POST {{graphqlUrl}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "query": "mutation($id: Int!, $name: String, $price: Decimal) { updateProduct(id: $id, name: $name, price: $price) { id name price } }",
  "variables": {
    "id": {{createdProductId}},
    "name": "Mouse Gamer Pro X",
    "price": 229.90
  }
}

### 5) Aplicar desconto em lote
POST {{graphqlUrl}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "query": "mutation($ids: [Int!]!, $discount: Decimal!) { applyDiscount(productIds: $ids, discountPercentage: $discount) { id name price } }",
  "variables": {
    "ids": [{{createdProductId}}],
    "discount": 10
  }
}

### 6) Excluir produto criado
POST {{graphqlUrl}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "query": "mutation($id: Int!) { deleteProduct(id: $id) }",
  "variables": {
    "id": {{createdProductId}}
  }
}

### 7) (Opcional) Excluir categoria criada
### Vai falhar se ainda houver produto vinculado nela.
POST {{graphqlUrl}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "query": "mutation($id: Int!) { deleteCategory(id: $id) }",
  "variables": {
    "id": {{createdCategoryId}}
  }
}

